From 0747a808cea2984eafe63cc7afc1c00cd62250cd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 21:54:41 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] skip libdecor plugins when nested

With BACKEND=wayland gamescope runs as a window and decorates it through
libdecor. Its plugins read org.freedesktop.appearance from the settings
portal with a blocking D-Bus call, and gamescope-session-plus hides the
portals with XDG_DESKTOP_PORTAL_DIR="", so the call hangs until the
startup socket times out. Point libdecor at an empty plugin directory so
the window goes undecorated. The DRM backend never takes this path, and
an explicit LIBDECOR_PLUGIN_DIR is respected.
---
 usr/share/gamescope-session-plus/gamescope-session-plus | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/usr/share/gamescope-session-plus/gamescope-session-plus b/usr/share/gamescope-session-plus/gamescope-session-plus
index 42094cb..84e7b88 100755
--- a/usr/share/gamescope-session-plus/gamescope-session-plus
+++ b/usr/share/gamescope-session-plus/gamescope-session-plus
@@ -226,6 +226,10 @@ if [ -z "$GAMESCOPECMD" ]; then
 	if [ -n "$BACKEND" ] && gamescope_has_option "--backend"; then
 		BACKEND_OPTION="--backend $BACKEND"
 	fi
+	# libdecor's plugins block on the portals this session hides.
+	if [ "$BACKEND" = "wayland" ] && [ -z "${LIBDECOR_PLUGIN_DIR:-}" ]; then
+		export LIBDECOR_PLUGIN_DIR=/nonexistent
+	fi
 	
 	MAX_SCALE_OPTION=""
 	if [ -n "$MAX_SCALE" ] && gamescope_has_option "--max-scale"; then
-- 
2.56.1

